<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{lang}}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>@data.status · @data.title</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    @* The error page: no URL of its own and no `load`. Its `data` is the error that brought the
       user here: `status`, `title`, `detail` when the server said something, `path` (what was
       asked, without the app's base), `back` (where the user came from, when it is of this app)
       and `home` (the app's home). `back` and `home` already carry the app's base: write them
       as they are in an `href`.
       With a layout: `<link rel="layout" href="../layouts/_layout.fud">`, one that needs no
       `load` to paint. *@
    <h1>@data.status · @data.title</h1>
    @if (data.detail !== undefined) {
      <p>@data.detail</p>
    }
    @if (data.back !== undefined) {
      <p><a href=@data.back>Back</a></p>
    } @else {
      <p><a href=@data.home>Home</a></p>
    }
  </body>
</html>
